URL path. 
Example: 
/students/101 
Here 101 is the student ID. 
@app.get("/students/{student_id}") 
def get_student(student_id: int): 
 return { 
 "student_id": student_id 
 }

2. GET 
GET is used to retrieve information. 
Example: 
@app.get("/students") 
def get_students(): 
 return { 
 "students": ["Arun", "Kumar", "Priya"] 
 } 
Request: 
GET /students 

3. POST 
POST is generally used to create new data. 
Example: 
@app.post("/students") 
def create_student(): 
 return { 
 "message": "Student created" 
 } 

4. PUT 
PUT is generally used to update or replace an existing resource. 
Example: 
@app.put("/students/101") 
def update_student():

return { 
 "message": "Student updated" 
 } 

5. PATCH 
PATCH is generally used when only part of a resource needs to be updated. 
Example: 
@app.patch("/students/101") 
def update_student_name(): 
 return { 
 "message": "Student name updated" 
 } 

6. DELETE 
DELETE is used to remove a resource. 
@app.delete("/students/101") 
def delete_student(): 
 return { 
 "message": "Student deleted" 
 } 

